---
import DocsLayout from "../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Variances"
  description="Document intentional departures from repository standards."
  current="/variances/"
>
  <article class="doc">
    <h1>Variances</h1>
    <p>
      Variances are not suppressions. They are reviewed departures from a
      standard, attached to exact subjects with required rationale. A variance
      remains visible in every report.
    </p>

    <pre><code>variances:
  src/parser/grammar.ts:
    kind: architectural
    reason: >
      Grammar definitions are intentionally centralized and easier to
      understand in a single file.
    metrics:
      scc.code_lines:
        max: 1274
      scc.complexity:
        max: 120
        reason: >
          Complexity is primarily driven by parser state generation.</code></pre>

    <h2>Exact subjects</h2>
    <p>
      Variances target exact repository-relative paths. The MVP intentionally
      avoids variance globs so each departure maps to one reviewed file.
    </p>

    <h2>Per-metric reasons</h2>
    <p>
      A variance has an overall reason, and individual metric overrides can add
      a more specific reason when the general rationale is not enough.
    </p>

    <h2>Adding from the CLI</h2>
    <pre><code>considered variance add \
  --subject src/parser/grammar.ts \
  --metric scc.code_lines \
  --kind architectural \
  --reason "Grammar definitions are intentionally centralized."</code></pre>

    <p>
      Adding a variance for a value that already satisfies its standard is
      rejected. The command is for reviewed exceptions, not noise.
    </p>
  </article>
</DocsLayout>
